<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:54:17 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>伦勃朗将古代神话变成“至高无上的人类”艺术作品。即将举办的展览追溯了他从古代汲取的灵感</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rembrandt-turned-ancient-myths-into-supremely-human-works-of-art-an-upcoming-exhibition-traces-the-inspiration-he-took-from-antiquity-180989705/</link><description>大都会艺术博物馆的“伦勃朗与古代人”将揭开这位荷兰大师职业生涯中“未被充分探索但至关重要”的部分，将他的画作与启发他们的前世进行对话</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:16:08 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rembrandt-turned-ancient-myths-into-supremely-human-works-of-art-an-upcoming-exhibition-traces-the-inspiration-he-took-from-antiquity-180989705/</guid></item><item><title>传说这位罗马皇帝在威尔士建立了一个营地。新发现的堡垒可能证明它确实存在</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/legend-has-it-that-this-roman-emperor-established-camp-wales-newly-discovered-fort-may-offer-proof-that-it-really-existed-180989702/</link><description>一位考古学家发现了一座与马格努斯·马克西姆斯有关的古代防御工事，马格努斯·马克西姆斯是一位四世纪的统治者，在中世纪的“马比诺吉翁”故事中以麦克森·韦尔迪格的名字永垂不朽。</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:51:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/legend-has-it-that-this-roman-emperor-established-camp-wales-newly-discovered-fort-may-offer-proof-that-it-really-existed-180989702/</guid></item><item><title>野生动物专家惊讶地发现禽流感杀死了深受喜爱的网络著名秃头鹰杰基</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/wildlife-experts-stunned-to-find-that-bird-flu-killed-jackie-the-beloved-internet-famous-bald-eagle-180989703/</link><description>杰基在加利福尼亚州奥海猛禽中心接受了数周的重症监护后于八月去世。尸检结果令人惊讶，因为杰基的症状对于禽流感来说并不常见，而且秃鹰之间没有持续爆发疫情</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:23:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/wildlife-experts-stunned-to-find-that-bird-flu-killed-jackie-the-beloved-internet-famous-bald-eagle-180989703/</guid></item><item><title>马德里翻新扩建的索罗拉博物馆让西班牙“光之大师”的画作重新出现在公众视野中</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/madrids-renewed-and-expanded-sorolla-museum-lets-the-paintings-of-the-spanish-master-of-light-reemerge-into-public-view-180989701/</link><description>该博物馆致力于展示华金·索罗拉·巴斯蒂达 (Joaquín Sorolla y Bastida) 的作品，以他历史悠久的住宅和工作室为中心。历时数年的改造第一阶段已完成，展览空间扩大</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:01:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/madrids-renewed-and-expanded-sorolla-museum-lets-the-paintings-of-the-spanish-master-of-light-reemerge-into-public-view-180989701/</guid></item><item><title>微塑料与无数人类健康问题有关。科学家可能终于弄清楚它们如何伤害身体</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/microplastics-have-been-linked-with-myriad-human-health-problems-scientists-may-have-finally-figured-out-how-they-harm-the-body-180989694/</link><description>实验室实验表明，微小的塑料碎片可以与我们体内的水发生反应，产生高活性分子。它们会导致破坏性的氧化应激和炎症</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:03:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/microplastics-have-been-linked-with-myriad-human-health-problems-scientists-may-have-finally-figured-out-how-they-harm-the-body-180989694/</guid></item><item><title>小型犬往往比大型犬活得更长。科学家表示他们可能终于知道原因了——而且已经深入到分子水平</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/small-dogs-tend-to-live-longer-than-big-dogs-scientists-say-they-might-finally-know-why-and-it-goes-to-the-molecular-level-180989695/</link><description>像大丹犬这样的大型犬种似乎比吉娃娃犬等小型犬种更快地在 DNA 上积累化学标签的变化。这些改变允许潜在有害的“跳跃基因”在其基因组中移动</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/small-dogs-tend-to-live-longer-than-big-dogs-scientists-say-they-might-finally-know-why-and-it-goes-to-the-molecular-level-180989695/</guid></item><item><title>这种古老的动物看起来像鸭嘴兽和水獭的杂交种。它提供了有关哺乳动物哺乳和吞咽起源的线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-ancient-animal-looked-like-a-platapys-otter-hybrid-its-providing-clues-about-the-origins-of-mammalian-suckling-and-swallowing-180989666/</link><description>这种重约两到四磅的掠食者在大约 1.65 亿年前与恐龙一起生活。在中国北方发现的化石表明，这种奇怪的生物具有令人惊讶的现代喉咙结构</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-ancient-animal-looked-like-a-platapys-otter-hybrid-its-providing-clues-about-the-origins-of-mammalian-suckling-and-swallowing-180989666/</guid></item><item><title>一幅 18 世纪波利尼西亚年轻人的纪念肖像——一件“最高艺术作品”——首次访问美国</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-monumental-18th-century-portrait-of-a-young-polynesian-man-a-supreme-work-of-art-visits-the-us-for-the-first-time-180989699/</link><description>巨幅《麦肖像》描绘了第一位访问英国的太平洋岛民，这位年轻人在参加探险家詹姆斯·库克的探险队后，在 1770 年代成为准名人</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-monumental-18th-century-portrait-of-a-young-polynesian-man-a-supreme-work-of-art-visits-the-us-for-the-first-time-180989699/</guid></item><item><title>官方消息：计时员已经摆脱了闰秒，并引入了闰时</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/its-official-timekeepers-have-gotten-rid-of-the-leap-second-and-introduced-the-leap-hour-instead-180989685/</link><description>自 1972 年以来，专家们在协调世界时的基础上增加了 27 秒，以使其与地球自转保持一致，但这并不是一个完美的解决方案</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:43:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/its-official-timekeepers-have-gotten-rid-of-the-leap-second-and-introduced-the-leap-hour-instead-180989685/</guid></item><item><title>在巴黎郊外的一座小岛上，一座被恰如其分地称为“大”的庞大当代艺术中心即将开业</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/on-an-island-outside-paris-a-sprawling-contemporary-arts-center-aptly-called-large-prepares-to-open-its-doors-180989690/</link><description>这个具有里程碑意义的机构的首次展览是为了向曾经在塞纳河塞金岛上运营的历史悠久的雷诺汽车工厂致敬。一位官员表示：“这个项目需要极大的毅力”</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:19:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/on-an-island-outside-paris-a-sprawling-contemporary-arts-center-aptly-called-large-prepares-to-open-its-doors-180989690/</guid></item><item><title>这位士兵在第一次世界大战的战壕里写了一本日记。几十年后，一个孩子在垃圾场发现了它，它被子弹击穿，沾满血迹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-soldier-kept-a-diary-in-the-trenches-of-world-war-i-a-child-found-it-at-the-dump-decades-later-pierced-by-a-bullet-and-stained-with-blood-180989696/</link><description>克洛德·纳托尔下士在日记中记录了他的战时经历。现在，经过几十年的研究，一位博物馆馆长在一本新书中讲述了这名士兵的故事</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:41:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-soldier-kept-a-diary-in-the-trenches-of-world-war-i-a-child-found-it-at-the-dump-decades-later-pierced-by-a-bullet-and-stained-with-blood-180989696/</guid></item><item><title>威尼斯艺术家卡纳莱托在这幅前所未见的素描中融合了幻想和建筑细节，本月即将拍卖</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/venetian-artist-canaletto-merged-fantasy-and-architectural-detail-in-this-previously-unseen-sketch-heading-to-auction-this-month-180989692/</link><description>这位 18 世纪的画家是“随想”艺术的主要实践者，这种艺术将日常生活场景与大胆、不合时宜的结构融为一体。这件作品在几个世纪以来一直不为人知，现在售价高达 80,000 美元</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:03:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/venetian-artist-canaletto-merged-fantasy-and-architectural-detail-in-this-previously-unseen-sketch-heading-to-auction-this-month-180989692/</guid></item><item><title>一张详细的火星漫游者照片突出显示了火星山脉之一边缘的神秘悬崖</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-detailed-martian-rover-photograph-highlights-mysterious-cliffs-on-the-edge-of-one-of-mars-mountains-180989675/</link><description>这些峭壁与山的其他部分不符，科学家们不知道它们是如何形成的</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:50:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-detailed-martian-rover-photograph-highlights-mysterious-cliffs-on-the-edge-of-one-of-mars-mountains-180989675/</guid></item><item><title>伦敦最古老的餐厅，君主和流行歌星都经常光顾，堪称“活生生的历史”。现在它受到国家信托基金的保护，为子孙后代服务</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/londons-oldest-restaurant-frequented-by-monarchs-and-pop-stars-alike-is-a-site-of-living-history-now-its-protected-by-the-national-trust-for-generations-to-come-180989688/</link><description>Rules 是一家历史悠久的餐厅，查尔斯·狄更斯 (Charles Dickens) 和麦当娜 (Madonna) 等人都曾在这里用餐，而这只是 200 多年来的第四次易手。游客可以看到布满文物的墙壁，并品尝丰富的英国美食</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:24:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/londons-oldest-restaurant-frequented-by-monarchs-and-pop-stars-alike-is-a-site-of-living-history-now-its-protected-by-the-national-trust-for-generations-to-come-180989688/</guid></item><item><title>野生动物生物学家开始为害羞信天翁手工接种疫苗，以防止禽流感在塔斯马尼亚的传播</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/wildlife-biologists-start-vaccinating-shy-albatross-by-hand-taking-aim-at-the-spread-of-avian-flu-in-tasmania-180989684/</link><description>如果一切按计划进行，官员们希望为信天翁岛上多达 100 只大型海鸟接种疫苗，每只接种两剂疫苗。之后，他们计划使用远程摄像头和后续访问来密切关注鸟类</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:21:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/wildlife-biologists-start-vaccinating-shy-albatross-by-hand-taking-aim-at-the-spread-of-avian-flu-in-tasmania-180989684/</guid></item><item><title>裤子里的鸟：迈阿密机场查获两名男子被控走私 21 只禽类</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/birds-in-their-pants-two-men-accused-of-smuggling-21-avians-after-miami-airport-bust-180989670/</link><description>海关官员表示，他们在这两名男子乘坐从古巴起飞的不同航班降落后，发现了藏在衣服里的生物，目前尚不清楚这两起事件是否有关联。野生动物贩运是世界第四大有组织犯罪形式</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:52:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/birds-in-their-pants-two-men-accused-of-smuggling-21-avians-after-miami-airport-bust-180989670/</guid></item><item><title>北达科他州州长官邸的建筑工程意外出土了七具可追溯到该州早期定居的棺材</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/construction-work-on-the-north-dakota-governors-residence-accidentally-unearthed-seven-coffins-dating-back-to-the-states-early-settlement-180989686/</link><description>该墓地建于 1872 年，当时州首府俾斯麦还是一个名为埃德温顿 (Edwinton) 的小型边境社区。五年后，大部分（但不是全部）墓地被挖掘出来，为铁路让路</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/construction-work-on-the-north-dakota-governors-residence-accidentally-unearthed-seven-coffins-dating-back-to-the-states-early-settlement-180989686/</guid></item><item><title>观看年度野生动物摄影师大赛的获奖者，捕捉大自然的壮丽和戏剧性</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-stunning-winners-of-the-wildlife-photographer-of-the-year-contest-capturing-the-splendor-and-drama-of-nature-180989681/</link><description>这 19 张公认的图像突出了我们星球的多样性以及欣赏和保护自然世界的价值</description><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:50:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-stunning-winners-of-the-wildlife-photographer-of-the-year-contest-capturing-the-splendor-and-drama-of-nature-180989681/</guid></item><item><title>在土耳其海岸发现了世界上最古老沉船的新竞争者。它的古代货物是 4,700 年前的“时间胶囊”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-contender-for-the-worlds-oldest-shipwreck-has-been-discovered-off-the-coast-of-turkey-its-ancient-cargo-is-a-time-capsule-from-4700-years-ago-180989682/</link><description>当这艘船沉入海底时，它可能正在穿越地中海运输大罐橄榄油或葡萄酒。一位考古学家“不敢相信里面还有多少”残留物</description><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:20:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-contender-for-the-worlds-oldest-shipwreck-has-been-discovered-off-the-coast-of-turkey-its-ancient-cargo-is-a-time-capsule-from-4700-years-ago-180989682/</guid></item><item><title>这幅文森特·梵高的画作已有 60 多年没有公开露面。它现在准备在即将举行的拍卖会上创下纪录</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-vincent-van-gogh-painting-has-not-been-seen-in-public-for-over-60-years-it-is-now-poised-to-set-a-record-at-an-upcoming-auction-180989680/</link><description>这位荷兰后印象派画家在他生命的最后几个月里创作了《盛开的栗树》。它即将作为“传奇”私人收藏的一部分进行拍卖，其中还包括塞尚和雷诺阿的作品</description><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:28:54 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-vincent-van-gogh-painting-has-not-been-seen-in-public-for-over-60-years-it-is-now-poised-to-set-a-record-at-an-upcoming-auction-180989680/</guid></item></channel></rss>